<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qutayba ibn Muslim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">669–715</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qutayba ibn Muslim was an Arab general and Umayyad governor of Khurasan from 705, appointed by al-Hajjaj. In a decade of campaigns he subdued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokharistan">Tokharistan</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> in 709 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> in 712, and raided into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fergana-valley">Ferghana</a>, bringing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> under Muslim rule. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-walid-i">al-Walid I</a> died in 715, Qutayba rebelled against his successor Sulayman and was killed by his own troops.</p></div>
